smoltcp 0.13.1: rate-limit neighbor discovery per address, not cache-wide.

Applied by scripts/vendor-smoltcp.sh. Upstream silences the whole neighbor
cache for a second after any ARP/NDP request, so resolving the gateway (for
DNS) holds back resolving a server on the same link. On the box that was
1.03 s of every first connection after association, measured 2026-09-24.

Each recently asked address keeps its own second of silence, so asking about
one neighbor never lifts another's. When more are pending than the cache has
room for, every unknown neighbor waits, as upstream does for all of them.

